{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the smallest perfect square strictly greater than integer n.\n    A perfect square is k*k for integer k >= 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    m = n if n >= 0 else 0\n    k = math.isqrt(m)\n    # k*k is the largest perfect square less than or equal to m (and thus n if n >= 0)\n    # We need the smallest perfect square strictly greater than n.\n    # If k*k is already > n, then k*k is our answer.\n    # Otherwise, we need (k+1)*(k+1).\n    if k * k > n:\n        return k * k\n    return (k + 1) * (k + 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "\nclass InputString:\n    def __init__(self, value: str) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n\n    def length(self) -> int:\n        return len(self.value)\n\nclass Subsequence:\n    def __init__(self, chars: str) -> None:\n        self.chars = chars\n        self.length = len(chars)\n\n    def isPalindrome(self) -> bool:\n        return self.chars == self.chars[::-1]\n\nclass LPSResult:\n    def __init__(self, length: int) -> None:\n        self.length = length\n\nclass LPSFunction:\n    def compute(self, input_str: \"InputString\") -> int:\n        s = input_str.value\n        n = input_str.length()\n\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j].\n        dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n        # All single characters are palindromes of length 1.\n        for i in range(n):\n            dp[i][i] = 1\n\n        # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n.\n        for length in range(2, n + 1):\n            for i in range(n - length + 1):\n                j = i + length - 1\n\n                if s[i] == s[j]:\n                    if length == 2:\n                        dp[i][j] = 2\n                    else:\n                        dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n        return dp[0][n - 1]\n\ndef lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    This function operates on raw characters; no normalization (case, whitespace, punctuation) is performed.\n    \"\"\"\n    input_obj = InputString(s)\n    lps_calculator = LPSFunction()\n    result_length = lps_calculator.compute(input_obj)\n    return result_length"}
