{"task_id": "Mbpp/471", "solution": "from typing import List\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass InputList:\n    elements: List[int]\n\n@dataclass\nclass Modulus:\n    n: int\n\n    def validate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates the modulus value, raising ValueError if n is not positive.\"\"\"\n        if self.n <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Modulus 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n@dataclass\nclass Result:\n    remainder: int\n\nclass ProductAccumulator:\n    \"\"\"Accumulates product with stepwise modular reduction.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, initial: int = 1):\n        self._value = initial\n\n    def multiply_mod(self, x: int, mod: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Multiplies the current accumulated value by x and applies modulo mod.\"\"\"\n        self._value = (self._value * x) % mod\n        return self._value\n\n    @property\n    def value(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the current accumulated value.\"\"\"\n        return self._value\n\ndef find_remainder(elements: List[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the product of array elements modulo n, applying modular reduction at each step.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not positive. Returns 1 % n for an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    modulus_obj = Modulus(n)\n    modulus_obj.validate()\n\n    input_list_obj = InputList(elements)\n\n    if not input_list_obj.elements:\n        # For an empty list, the product is 1 (multiplicative identity).\n        return 1 % n\n\n    accumulator = ProductAccumulator(initial=1)\n    for element in input_list_obj.elements:\n        accumulator.multiply_mod(element, n)\n\n    result_obj = Result(remainder=accumulator.value)\n    return result_obj.remainder"}
